From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:27:35 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: serial: samsung: Add Apple S8000 UART
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The S8000 (A9) UARTs program UBRDIV with the divisor and the
oversampling selector like the T8010 ones; the Bluetooth UART of the
iPad 5 needs that to reach 3 Mbit/s. Add apple,s8000-uart with
apple,t8010-uart and apple,s5l-uart as fallbacks, so the driver uses
the existing T8010 data and no driver change is needed.

Signed-off-by: Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
[Orchard: from brkosebay/linux 57ff1534 (J71t ledger 6.19); dropped
 the separate apple,s8000-uart driver match entry and made
 apple,t8010-uart a fallback compatible instead]
Co-developed-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Signed-off-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/serial/samsung_uart.yaml | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/serial/samsung_uart.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/serial/samsung_uart.yaml
index df763d5ae..67d0ee9b4 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/serial/samsung_uart.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/serial/samsung_uart.yaml
@@ -31,6 +31,10 @@ properties:
       - items:
           - const: apple,t8010-uart
           - const: apple,s5l-uart
+      - items:
+          - const: apple,s8000-uart
+          - const: apple,t8010-uart
+          - const: apple,s5l-uart
       - items:
           - const: samsung,exynos2200-uart
           - const: google,gs101-uart
